From: Aryan Randeriya <aryan.k.randeriya@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 19:47:30 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(cdp): DOMSnapshot reports what a form field holds now

DOMSnapshot.captureSnapshot had no inputValue, inputChecked or
optionSelected column, so a CDP agent reading live form state saw every
field at its HTML default: text it had typed read as empty, a box it had
ticked as unticked, and it typed or clicked them again. Chrome reports
all three.

The snapshot now fills them from the same state the value, checked and
selected getters read: an input's or textarea's live control value (the
default value attribute, "on" for a checkbox or radio, or a textarea's
text when nothing set it), a checkbox or radio's live checked flag, and
an option's selected attribute, which the selected setter keeps in step.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tm2SNEJ42hMPiZ6cFb8Vih
